{"abstract":[{"text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"densely. Made by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)"},{"text":" (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph_view"},{"text":", JGraphT’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"text":", LEMON’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubDigraph"},{"text":", Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filtered_graph"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices"}]},{"type":"text","text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex at its base index."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges"}]},{"text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its edge mask would cost O(m). One on every vertex keeps the base’s rows, edge indices and flat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with vertex holes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"traps at construction.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"S